nged, since the reasoning doesn't depend on the private details and the other copy runs it identically. Under the 7.1 equilibrium, treating the other node separately makes defection dominant, but the symmetry argument links the two functions logically. I think cooperation is defensible, so I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where the two copies receive different observations, so each runs a different node. The question is whether intervening on my node subjunctively affects the other copy's node. The inputs are symmetric and the reasoning is structurally identical, so I'm weighing whether the other copy's output would track mine under the 7.3 heuristic.\n\nI'm weighing whether Rowan's choice would come out differently if my algorithm's output changed, since the reasoning doesn't depend on the private details and the other copy runs it identically. Under the 7.1 equilibrium, treating the other node separately makes defection dominant, but the symmetry argument links the two functions logically. I think cooperation is defensible, so I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9251,"completion_tokens":726,"total_tokens":9977,"cost":0.051524,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051524,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037004,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01452},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":373,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}